{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MulOppositeSemisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MulOppositeSemisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Opposite","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Equiv"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MulOppositeSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRing_mulOpposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MulOppositeSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRing_mulOpposite","kind":"instance","line":10,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MulOppositeSemisimple.lean#L10-L34","doc":"**`IsSemisimpleRing Rᵐᵒᵖ`** — Mathlib's `proof_wanted\nIsSemisimpleRing.mulOpposite`.\n\n`IsSemisimpleRing R` is `IsSemisimpleModule R R`, i.e. semisimplicity as a\n**left** module; `Rᵐᵒᵖ` semisimple is the right-handed statement. That the two\nagree is a theorem, not a definitional shuffle, and Artin–Wedderburn is what\nsupplies it: the decomposition is a product of matrix rings over division\nrings, and each of those three constructions commutes with `ᵐᵒᵖ`.\n\n    Rᵐᵒᵖ  ≃+*  (Π i, Matrix dᵢ dᵢ Dᵢ)ᵐᵒᵖ        `RingEquiv.op` of AW\n          ≃+*  Π i, (Matrix dᵢ dᵢ Dᵢ)ᵐᵒᵖ         `RingEquiv.piMulOpposite`\n          ≃+*  Π i, Matrix dᵢ dᵢ Dᵢᵐᵒᵖ           `RingEquiv.mopMatrix.symm`\n\nand `Dᵢᵐᵒᵖ` is again a division ring (`MulOpposite.instDivisionRing`), so each\nblock is semisimple by `MatrixSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}